nvidia-kmod-open (615.71.09-2+stereo3d8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * debian/sparky-lean-payload-sources.json maps /usr/src/nvidia-615.71.09 to
    the source tree, so lean.debhelper restores the authored text of the
    installed copy by path, not by content hash (ORDER 311). Without it, the
    toolkit 0.1.15 build of +stereo3d6 filled three files the source ships
    empty (src/nvidia/interface/nvRmReg.h,
    src/nvidia/generated/g_kern_hwpm_power_nvoc.c,
    g_kern_hwpm_common_defs_nvoc.c) with the comment of other generated files:
    a content-hash restore cannot tell an originally empty file from a comment-
    only one the native pass made empty. tests/payload-map-proof.sh shows it.
  * Correction to +stereo3d7's second item: its binary packages were built
    fresh from that source (nothing compiles in this DKMS package), not re-
    projected from the +stereo3d6 HR companion; the fresh build is what left
    those three files empty, as the source has them (ORDER 311).
  * Built with the Lean Code toolkit 0.1.21 of build-repo main cb9f644: C and
    C++ files lose their comment-only lines, with no #line directive and no
    empty line where a comment was; dpkg-stereo --resolve finds a lean line's
    authored line by its content (ORDER 334).

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 00:37:01 -0300

